    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, the only concrete test class) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for a derived `timezone` field returned as an IANA name, mapped from the owner's region/locality: `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`.\n\nI implemented it as a purely derived response field, following the existing `locality` pattern, across three files:\n\n1. **`Timezone.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained helper in `rest/function/owner` (mirroring `AgeBand`, `MembershipLevel`, etc.) with one static `of(region)` switch mapping the three pinned regions to IANA names, and `null` otherwise (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema, next to `locality`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` line on `toOwnerDto`, reusing the same `customerCode`-prefix region extraction that feeds `locality` and delegating the mapping to `Timezone.of(...)`.\n\nNo entity, repository, or OfficeFloor YAML changes were needed \u2014 the paged v2 endpoint inherits the field automatically through the shared mapper.\n\n**Structural impact:** behaviour lives in a new cohesive unit with zero surrounding complexity (`WMC_other = 0`); the only edit to existing logic is a single annotation line on the interface method `toOwnerDto` (its cyclomatic complexity unchanged). No existing method or class was grown.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`, including the driving `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` test asserting `locality=NSW` and `timezone=Australia/Sydney`.",
